    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDating back to 1840's and part of the former Butler Estate, The Lodge is a beautifully restored three-bedroom detached former gate lodge, situated in the tranquil countryside setting of Castlecrine, just 3 km from Sixmilebridge. Originally part of the historic Castlecrine Estate and extensively restored in the 1990s, this distinctive stone-built residence retains many original features, including its turret, arched windows, exposed stone walls, timber windows and doors, and parapet roof detailing.\n\nExtending to approximately 103.57 sq. m., the accommodation comprises an entrance hallway with feature timber staircase, two reception rooms, a fitted kitchen, ground-floor WC, two spacious bedrooms with built-in wardrobes and a main bathroom. The property benefits from updated wiring and plumbing, a modern oil-fired central heating boiler, mains water and a septic tank.\n\nAccessed through a gated entrance with traditional cut-stone boundary walls, the property enjoys a wraparound gravel driveway, lawns on all sides and an abundance of mature trees. Sixmilebridge offers excellent amenities, including schools, shops, cafés and a railway station, while the nearby M18 provides convenient access to Shannon, Limerick, Ennis and Galway.\n\nCombining historic character with modern comforts, The Lodge presents a rare opportunity to acquire a distinctive period home in a peaceful countryside setting.\n\nViewing strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents DNG O'Sullivan Hurley. PSL 002295."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hallway - 6.15m x 2m\nPolished flag flooring, rear aspect window, built-in storage, timber u shaped stairs leading to first floor landing, exposed stone feature to part of the walls. door to reception one, kitchen, bedroom one and under stairs wc.\n\nMain Reception - 3.60m x 3.60m\nTimber flooring, front aspect window, rough plaster walls with a stone wall feature, integrated wall exposed shelving. solid fuel stove on raised flag with tile insert and timber surround and wall mounted lighting.\n\nKitchen - 3.60m x 3.60m\nFlag flooring, rear aspect window, rear door access, built-in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, eye level glass display units, single drainer sink, space for cooker with tile splash back and overhead extractor hood and fan, exposed stone wall shelf and space and plumbing for washing machine, dryer, dishwasher and fridge.\n\nGround Floor WC - 2.1m x 1.5m\nFlag flooring, low level wc and wash hand basin with base vanity unit.\n\nBedroom One / Reception Room Two - 4.8m x 3m\nSolid timber flooring, dual aspect windows to front and sided, built-in display unit with base shelving, separate integrated exposed shelving and wall mounted lighting.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 3.60m x 3.09m\nTimber flooring, rear aspect window, door to hot press and doors to bedroom two, three and main bathroom.\n\nMain Bathroom - 2.10m x 1.65m\nFully tiled ceiling to floor, side aspect window, low level wc, wash hand basin, with overhead electric shaver point and light and corner fitted shower tray with overhead electric shower.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.60m x 3.60m\nSolid timber flooring, rear aspect window, wall mounted lighting and ceiling to floor and wall to wall built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and storage.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.60m x 3.60m\nSolid timber flooring, front aspect window, wall mounted lighting and ceiling to floor and wall to wall built-in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and storage.\n\n"
      },
